# [[Genomics]]
# [[Bioinformatics]]
# [[Biological sequence]]
# [[Sequence alignment]]
# [[Biological database]]
# [[Sequence annotation]]
# [[Phylogenetics]]
# [[Systems biology]]
# [[Reproducible computational research]]

== Title decisions ==

* [[Genetics]], [[Genomics]], [[Bioinformatics]], [[Biological sequence]], [[Sequence alignment]], [[Biological database]], [[Sequence annotation]], [[Phylogenetics]], and [[Systems biology]] remain established broad public titles.
* '''[[Reproducible bioinformatics workflow]] → [[Reproducible computational research]]'''. The narrower requested title describes one domain-specific instance. The canonical page should capture the durable cross-domain computational practice while retaining bioinformatics as a major use case.
* [[Reproducible computational research]] remains distinct from existing [[Reproducibility]]: the former is a method/practice layer; the latter is the general scientific property/goal.

== Domain decision ==

No new controlled Domain is introduced.

Wave 12 uses:

* Biology
* Science
* Computer science
* Mathematics
* Systems science

== Dependency graph ==

<pre>
Genetics
 └→ Genomics
      ├→ Bioinformatics
      │    ├→ Biological sequence
      │    │    ├→ Sequence alignment
      │    │    └→ Sequence annotation
      │    ├→ Biological database
      │    └→ Reproducible computational research
      ├→ Phylogenetics
      └→ Systems biology
</pre>

This is an explanatory graph, not a strict subclass hierarchy.

== Required non-equivalences ==

<pre>
genetics ≠ genomics
gene influence ≠ genetic determinism
genomics ≠ sequencing only
bioinformatics ≠ sequence analysis only
bioinformatics ≠ any computer use in biology
biological sequence ≠ physical molecule
sequence ≠ annotation
alignment ≠ proof of homology
sequence similarity ≠ homology
biological database ≠ static file collection
database record ≠ verified truth
predicted annotation ≠ experimentally validated function
phylogenetic tree ≠ directly observed history
gene tree ≠ species tree
systems biology ≠ network diagram
reproducible computational research ≠ general reproducibility
reproducibility ≠ replication
open code ≠ reproducible workflow
</pre>

== Source families ==

* NHGRI / NIH — genetics and genomics definitions.
* NCBI / GenBank / Bookshelf — bioinformatics, biological sequences, alignment, databases, annotation.
* EMBL-EBI — current bioinformatics and sequence-analysis practice/resources.
* Yang & Rannala and statistical phylogenetics literature — phylogenetic inference and uncertainty.
* NIH/NIGMS and systems-biology literature — dynamic integrative biological systems.
* Sandve et al.; Piccolo & Frampton; FAIR principles; Nature Methods — reproducible computational research.

== Cross-wave links ==

* [[Causality]], [[Probability]], [[Uncertainty]], [[Measurement]], and [[Scientific model]] ground biological inference.
* [[Database]], [[Metadata]], [[Provenance]], [[Algorithm]], [[Software]], and [[Version control]] ground bioinformatics.
* [[Information]], [[Network]], [[Feedback]], [[Complex system]], [[System boundary]], and [[Adaptation (systems)]] connect to systems biology.
* [[Reproducibility]], [[Replication]], and [[Validation]] remain distinct from the computational practices introduced here.

